  <datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"... Her book Golden Lotus references a popular Chinese origin story of the custom of foot-binding, telling the history of the practice within a historical and personal context. The book features a dos-à-dos binding. One side features a pop-up golden lotus made with handmade paper using lotus root, kozo, and cotton fibers. The images on the petals are from a 1970s X-ray of bound feet combined with X-ray images of the artist's own feet, and are printed with polyester lithography plates. The other side is a six page booklet featuring text, and photographs taken by the artist on a trip to China in 2014. These images are printed using photo polymer intaglio plates."--Publisher's description, https://wsworkshop.org/collection/golden-lotus/, viewed 6/1/2023.</subfield>
  </datafield>
